\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 What's New\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 The framework has been extended substantially in the recent releases:\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 1.\tab Deep learning model zoo (Data_science/MachineLearning/) \u8212? modern neural architectures\line implemented in pure managed code: CNN, RNN, Transformer, ANN (in the DeepLearning package),\line plus dedicated packages for GNN (graph neural networks: GCN / GAT / temporal graphs),\line LNN (liquid neural networks with ODE-solver cells), SNN (spiking neural networks: LIF\line neurons, surrogate gradients, STDP), VAE, RBM, DBN and Deep-Q-Network.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 2.\tab LLM engine (llm/) \u8212? a decoder-only language model built on the Transformer architecture:\line DeepSeek-style MoE routing, KV cache incremental decoding, RoPE, RMSNorm, SwiGLU,\line GQA/MQA, function calling with schema-constrained decoding and a full agent loop.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 3.\tab NumericTable unified data model (Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/src/Data/NumericTable.vb) \u8212?\line one table model (row names + feature columns + label columns) shared by every machine-learning\line algorithm in the framework, enabling chain-style data-science pipelines:\line NumericTableIO.ReadCsv(...).kmeans(3).pca(2).ScoreTable() \u8230?\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 4.\tab SIMD math acceleration (Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/src/Math/SIMD/) \u8212? hardware-vectorized\line arithmetic (SSE2/AVX/ARM Advanced SIMD) for element-wise math, matrix kernels and reductions,\line plus a Vec* operator vocabulary used by the script engine's auto-vectorization.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 5.\tab CUDA GPU framework (cuda/) \u8212? ILCuda (P/Invoke of the CUDA Driver API + NVRTC runtime\line compilation, zero third-party dependencies, and an IL \u8594? CUDA translator that compiles your\line .NET methods to GPU kernels) and ILCudaTensor (a double-precision GPU tensor runtime whose\line CudaTensor transparently switches the whole Tensor/nn operator family to the GPU).\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 6.\tab The VBS script engine (vs_solutions/VBS/) \u8212? run VB.NET scripts directly:\line no project, no compilation step, no deployment. The engine parses, restructures, compiles\line in memory via Roslyn and executes the assembly \u8212? and adds scripting-only syntax extensions\line (vectorized array math, let dynamic typing, tuple destructuring, @ array projection,\line #include of dlls/scripts/NuGet packages).\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 Features\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Extended VisualBasic syntax \u8212? Value(Of T) inline assignment, List(Of T) with a + append\line operator and rich indexers, LINQ helpers (Sequence, Iterates, which, sentinel) and Unix-shell\line style helpers (UnixBash.ls, cat).\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Command-line application framework \u8212? attribute-driven (<ExportAPI>, <Usage>) CLIs, automatic\line help generation, and InteropService to host external command-line tools.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab VB.NET script engine (vbs) \u8212? top-level statements, ?"--arg" parameters, #include\line (assembly / script / NuGet), magic methods (Here(), ScriptDir()), auto-vectorized numeric\line array math, print data inspection in GNU R style, and make-project to promote a debugged\line script into a real .vbproj project.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Unified tabular model \u8212? NumericTable \u8212? row names + feature columns + label columns, with\line chainable extension methods shared across K-Means, PCA, hierarchical clustering, linear/polynomial\line fitting, UMAP/PaCMAP, SHAP and more.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Deep learning \u8212? CNN (Conv2D/Pooling/Dropout/\u8230? + Softmax/SVM/Regression losses), char-level RNN,\line encoder\u8211?decoder Transformer with multi-head attention, feed-forward ANN, GCN/GAT graph networks,\line liquid time-constant networks, spiking neural networks, VAE/RBM/DBN, DQN reinforcement learning.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab LLM inference & training \u8212? decoder-only Transformer with MoE experts, KV cache prefill +\line incremental decoding, RoPE positional embedding, AdamW trainer, sampling strategies and\line schema-constrained function calling (agent loop).\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Classic machine learning \u8212? K-Means, hierarchical clustering, SVM, decision trees / random forest\line (Bonsai), Na\u239?ve Bayes, HMM, XGBoost-style gradient boosting, association rules, sequence alignment,\line SHAP value explanation.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Dimension reduction & manifold learning \u8212? PCA, UMAP, PaCMAP, t-SNE.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab GPU heterogeneous computing \u8212? CUDA Driver API interop, NVRTC kernel compilation, device memory\line & streams, BLAS/reduction/element-wise kernels, IL\u8594?CUDA source translation, and a\line GPU tensor runtime with automatic backend switching.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab SIMD vectorized math \u8212? System.Numerics.Vector-based element-wise arithmetic, matrix kernels\line (SimdMatrix), reductions (SimdReduce) and math functions (SimdMath) for float/double data.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Scientific file I/O \u8212? NetCDF, HDF5, Feather, SQLite3, HDSPack, msgpack and other binary formats,\line plus MIME text/XML and Excel (OpenXML) parsing.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Mathematics \u8212? linear algebra, statistics & hypothesis testing (ANOVA), data fitting /\line bootstrapping, Gibbs sampling, signal processing, symbolic math and ODE solvers (Runge\u8211?Kutta,\line SUNDIALS CVODE bindings).\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Evolutionary algorithms \u8212? genetic algorithms and differential evolution under\line Microsoft.VisualBasic.MachineLearning.Darwinism.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Natural-language processing \u8212? word2vec, TextRank keyword extraction, KnowledgeGraph and the\line GraphQuery object query DSL.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Visualization / "Graphics Artist" \u8212? scatter, line, bar, histogram, heatmap, volcano and 3-D\line plots; network/force-directed layouts; SVG / d3js / PDF export; colorbrewer palettes; isometric 3-D\line engine; AVI video writing; Gaussian splatting 3D. Figures are tuned for printable,\line publication-quality output.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab LLM proxy \u8212? bridge a local model (e.g. Ollama) or any Func(Of String, String) endpoint into the\line runtime via Microsoft.VisualBasic.LLMs.\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 Installation & Build\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Prerequisites\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab .NET 10 SDK (the libraries target net10.0; graphics/imaging projects additionally\line target net10.0-windows).\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Visual Studio 2022 (Windows) or any editor with the VB.NET / .NET workload (Visual Studio Code +\line the C#/VB dev kit, or JetBrains Rider) on Linux / macOS.\par
\pard\ql\li360\tx360\fi-360\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 \u8226?\tab Optional: an NVIDIA GPU + driver for the cuda/ acceleration layer (everything else runs CPU-only).\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Consume the packages\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 The individual libraries are published as NuGet packages under the Microsoft.VisualBasic.* family (e.g. the core runtime assembly Microsoft.VisualBasic.Runtime). Add them to your project with:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 dotnet add package Microsoft.VisualBasic.Runtime\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Build from source\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Clone the repository and build the NuGet solution, which references every library project:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 git clone https://github.com/xieguigang/sciBASIC.git\line cd sciBASIC\line dotnet build nuget.slnx -c Release\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 To build a single library, open its .vbproj (for example Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/src/Core.vbproj, llm/llm.vbproj or vs_solutions/VBS/VBS.vbproj) or the relevant solution under vs_solutions/.\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 Quick Start\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 A. Classic sciBASIC# console application\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.ApplicationServices\line Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.CommandLine\line Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.CommandLine.Reflection\line \line Module Program\line \line     Public Function Main() As Integer\line         ' Standard sciBASIC# CLI entry point: dispatches /switch based on\line         ' <ExportAPI> methods and auto-generates the help screen.\line         Return GetType(Program).RunCLI(App.CommandLine)\line     End Function\line \line     <ExportAPI("/hello")>\line     <Usage("/hello /name <string>")>\line     Public Function Hello(args As CommandLine) As Integer\line         Call Console.WriteLine($"Hello, \{args("/name")\}!")\line         Return 0\line     End Function\line \line End Module\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 yourapp.exe /hello /name "sciBASIC#"\line # -> Hello, sciBASIC#!\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 B. Or just write a script \u8212? no project needed\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Save hello.vb:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 ' No Module, no Sub Main \u8212? top-level statements just work.\line Dim name As String = ?"--name"      ' read a command-line argument\line \line Call Console.WriteLine($"Hello, \{name\}!")\line \line Dim x = \{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\}\line Call print(x * 2 + 1)               ' vectorized array math, R-style output\line ' [1]  3  5  7  9 11\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Run it with the vbs host (see The VBS Script Engine):\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 dotnet build vs_solutions/VBS/VBS.vbproj -c Release\line .nuget/net10.0/vbs.exe hello.vb --name "sciBASIC#"\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 NumericTable \u8212? One Data Model for the Whole Data-Science Pipeline\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/src/Data/NumericTable.vb defines the framework's unified 2-D data model: row names + feature columns + label columns (labels are the label:-prefixed columns). Every machine-learning algorithm in sciBASIC# understands this model, so data flows between algorithms without conversion glue code \u8212? you simply chain the steps.\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data\line \line ' 1. Load a csv (row names + D1..D4 feature columns; text class column ignored)\line Dim table = NumericTableIO.ReadCsv("bezdekIris.csv", columns := \{"D1","D2","D3","D4"\})\line \line ' 2. K-Means clustering writes its result back into the table's label matrix\line Dim result = table.kmeans(k := 3)\line \line ' 3. PCA on the clustered table -> project to the first two components\line Dim score = result.pca(maxPC := 2).ScoreTable()\line \line ' 4. Pull columns for plotting\line Dim pc1 = score.Feature("PC1")\line Dim pc2 = score.Feature("PC2")\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 (excerpt from tutorials/VBS/scripts/kmeans/kmeans.vb \u8212? a complete Iris clustering + PCA + scatter-plot demo)\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Regression works the same way:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Dim model = table.LinearFit(y := "y")          ' linear regression on the label column\line Dim quad  = table.PolyFit(poly_n := 2)         ' polynomial comparison model\line Dim out   = table.SetPrediction(model, withResidual := True)   ' new table + prediction/residual labels\line \line Call out.WriteCsv("fit.csv")\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 (excerpt from tutorials/VBS/scripts/linear_regression/linear_regression.vb)\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Key API surface: nsamples / nfeatures / nlabels, Feature(name), GetLabel(name), SetLabel(name, values), Slice(rows), Select(cols), Clone(), plus IO helpers (NumericTableIO.ReadCsv, WriteCsv) and R-style print(tbl) table rendering.\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
