\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 LLM Engine (Decoder-Only Transformer)\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 llm/llm.vbproj provides a pure-managed decoder-only language model covering three main lines beside the classic encoder\u8211?decoder Transformer in DeepLearning:\par
\trowd\trgaph120\trleft0\trrh0\trhdr\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clcbpat5\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clcbpat5\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clcbpat5\cellx9024\pard\intbl\ql\cbpat5\plain\f0\af1\fs22\b\cf7 Line\cell\pard\intbl\ql\cbpat5\plain\f0\af1\fs22\b\cf7 Types\cell\pard\intbl\ql\cbpat5\plain\f0\af1\fs22\b\cf7 What it does\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph120\trleft0\trrh0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\cellx9024\pard\intbl\ql\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Mixture of Experts\cell\pard\intbl\ql\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 MoELayer\cell\pard\intbl\ql\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 DeepSeekMoE: fine-grained expert splitting + shared expert isolation + Sigmoid Top-K routing + auxiliary-loss-free load balancing + node-limited routing\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph120\trleft0\trrh0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clcbpat6\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clcbpat6\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clcbpat6\cellx9024\pard\intbl\ql\cbpat6\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 KV Cache\cell\pard\intbl\ql\cbpat6\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 KVCache, CausalSelfAttention\cell\pard\intbl\ql\cbpat6\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 prefill + incremental decoding \u8212? per-step attention cost drops from O(t\u178?) to O(t); nKvHeads < nHeads gives GQA/MQA\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph120\trleft0\trrh0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\cellx9024\pard\intbl\ql\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Function calling\cell\pard\intbl\ql\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 ToolCallProtocol, JsonSchema, ConstrainedDecoder, ToolRegistry, AgentLoop\cell\pard\intbl\ql\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 tool schema injection \u8594? constrained decoding (schema compiled to a finite-state machine, illegal tokens masked to -inf) \u8594? parse \u8594? execute \u8594? feed back \u8594? multi-turn loop\cell\row
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Supporting modules: RmsNorm, RotaryEmbedding (RoPE), SwiGLUFeedForward, LLMBlock, LLMModel, Sampler, LMTrainer (AdamW, warmup + cosine schedule, gradient clipping), ParameterSet, TokenStream, TokenizerVocabulary. No automatic differentiation framework \u8212? backprop is hand-written per component against cached forward snapshots, keeping the whole engine readable and debuggable.\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 ' Build & train (see TalkBuddy/test/Program.vb for the full walkthrough:\line ' pretraining -> instruction SFT -> tool-call SFT -> MoE routing stats\line ' -> sampling comparison -> KV-cache consistency -> multi-turn tool calling)\line Dim model As New LLMModel(New LLMModelConfig With \{.dModel = 512, .nLayers = 8, ...\})\line Dim trainer As New LMTrainer(model, New AdamW(model.Parameters, lr:=0.0003))\line Call trainer.TrainStep(batch)\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 GPU Acceleration \u8212? ILCuda & ILCudaTensor\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 The cuda/ root brings native NVIDIA GPU heterogeneous computing to sciBASIC# \u8212? with zero third-party NuGet dependencies (it P/Invokes nvcuda.dll and nvrtc64_*.dll directly).\par
\trowd\trgaph120\trleft0\trrh0\trhdr\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clcbpat5\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clcbpat5\cellx9026\pard\intbl\ql\cbpat5\plain\f0\af1\fs22\b\cf7 Project\cell\pard\intbl\ql\cbpat5\plain\f0\af1\fs22\b\cf7 Role\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph120\trleft0\trrh0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\cellx9026\pard\intbl\ql\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 cuda/ILCuda/ILCuda.vbproj\cell\pard\intbl\ql\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 CUDA compute framework: device/context/stream management, device memory & pinned host buffers, NVRTC multi-pass kernel compilation, kernel registry & launch planning, built-in reduction / element-wise / BLAS (GEMM, GEMV) kernels, structured diagnostics. Includes IL2Cuda: an IL \u8594? AST \u8594? CUDA-C translator with <CudaKernel>/<CudaInput>/<CudaOutput> attributes that turns ordinary .NET methods into GPU kernels.\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph120\trleft0\trrh0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clcbpat6\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf2\clcbpat6\cellx9026\pard\intbl\ql\cbpat6\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 cuda/ILCudaTensor/ILCudaTensor.vbproj\cell\pard\intbl\ql\cbpat6\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 GPU tensor runtime: device-resident CudaTensor (dense + CSR sparse storage) and a set of double-precision kernels (GEMM, softmax, reductions, conv/pool, sparse\u215?dense). One Register() call switches the whole TensorFlow-style Tensor/Math/nn operator family to the GPU backend \u8212? operators without a GPU kernel silently fall back to the CPU implementation, so nothing ever breaks.\cell\row
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 ' After one registration, tensor math runs on the GPU automatically:\line Call CudaTensor.Register()\line \line Dim a = Tensor.Random(2048, 2048)\line Dim b = Tensor.Random(2048, 2048)\line Dim c = a * b      ' GEMM on the GPU, double precision\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 The ILCuda test project doubles as a demo CLI:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 dotnet ILCuda.Demo.dll info        # device & NVRTC environment probe (with memory info)\line dotnet ILCuda.Demo.dll demo        # pearson-correlation + euclidean-distance matrices on GPU\line dotnet ILCuda.Demo.dll selftest    # kernel-logic self-check (no GPU required)\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 SIMD Math Acceleration\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/src/Math/SIMD/ is the CPU-side high-performance math core, used by the machine-learning packages and by the script engine's auto-vectorizer:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 SIMD/\line \u9500?\u9472?\u9472? SimdEngine.vb          # capability detection & dispatch (SSE2 / AVX / ARM Advanced SIMD)\line \u9500?\u9472?\u9472? SimdMath.vb            # vectorized math functions (sqrt, exp, log, abs, ...)\line \u9500?\u9472?\u9472? SimdMatrix.vb          # matrix kernels\line \u9500?\u9472?\u9472? SimdReduce.vb          # sum / min / max / mean reductions (sequential, reproducible floats)\line \u9500?\u9472?\u9472? SimdCompare.vb / SimdCapabilities.vb\line \u9500?\u9472?\u9472? SimdExtensions.vb      # Simd* extension vocabulary\line \u9500?\u9472?\u9472? Vectorized.vb          # the Vec* operator vocabulary (VecAdd / VecMultiply / VecSum / ...)\line \u9500?\u9472?\u9472? Arithmetic/            # Add / Subtract / Multiply / Divide / Modulo / Exponent facades\line \u9492?\u9472?\u9472? Parallel/              # block-parallel variants\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Script authors rarely call these directly \u8212? when a script performs arithmetic on numeric arrays, the VBS engine rewrites the expression tree into Vec* calls (see below), which resolve to these SIMD kernels at runtime.\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 The VBS Script Engine\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 vs_solutions/VBS/VBS.vbproj builds the vbs scripting host: run a .vb file directly, without creating a VS project or compiling an exe. The engine textually parses and restructures the script, compiles it in memory through Roslyn, executes it via reflection inside a collectible AssemblyLoadContext (fully unloaded afterwards), and never touches disk.\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 vbs ./run.vb --a=123 --flag          # run a script with arguments\line vbs ./run.vb --verbose               # print the generated compilable code + debug build\line vbs ./run.vb --no-vectorize          # disable auto-vectorization\line vbs make-project ./run.vb            # promote the script into a real vbproj project\par
