\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 A complete data-science script\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 tutorials/VBS/scripts/kmeans/kmeans.vb \u8212? Iris clustering + PCA + chart export, runnable as-is:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 #include "Microsoft.VisualBasic.DataMining.Framework.dll"\line #include "Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.Framework.dll"\line #include "Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.DataPlot.dll"\line #include "Microsoft.VisualBasic.Math.Statistics.ANOVA.dll"\line #include "Microsoft.VisualBasic.Drawing.dll"\line \line imports microsoft.visualbasic.data\line imports microsoft.visualbasic.datamining.kmeans\line imports microsoft.visualbasic.data.plots\line imports microsoft.visualbasic.drawing\line \line dim file = here("../../data/bezdekIris.csv")      ' magic method: relative to the script\line dim k = 3\line \line dim table = NumericTableIO.ReadCsv(file, columns := \{"D1","D2","D3","D4"\})\line dim result = table.kmeans(k := k)                  ' clustering via the unified table model\line dim score = result.pca(maxPC := 2).ScoreTable()    ' PCA projection\line \line dim pc1 = score.Feature("PC1")\line dim pc2 = score.Feature("PC2")\line ' ... build a ScatterPlot and save a PNG next to the script ...\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Run it:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 cd .nuget/net10.0\line vbs.exe G:\\GCModeller\\src\\runtime\\sciBASIC#\\tutorials\\VBS\\scripts\\kmeans\\kmeans.vb\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 The tutorials/VBS/scripts/ folder contains many more runnable demos, most with expected output (stdout.txt) and generated figures: linear_regression, word2vec (word vectors + UMAP + K-Means), hola_layout (orthogonal network layout), mnist_cnn, spiking_nn, tf-idf, hierarchical_clustering, mnist_umap, dynamic_type, tuple.\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 VBS.vbproj can also be embedded as a class library:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports VBScriptHost.Script\line \line Dim vbs As ScriptParseResult = VBScript.ParseScript("./run.vb")\line \line Using runtime As ScriptRuntime = vbs.CompileScript()\line     Dim exitCode As Integer = runtime.Run(\{"--a", "123"\})\line End Using   ' the dynamic assembly is unloaded here\par
