\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 Extended VisualBasic Language\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 sciBASIC# extends the VB.NET surface so that small data-science scripts read almost like a domain-specific language. All of the helpers below live in Microsoft.VisualBasic.Language (core runtime) unless noted.\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Inline value assignment \u8212? Value(Of T)\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Language\line \line Dim line As Value(Of String) = ""\line \line ' inline assignment\line Do While (line = stream.ReadLine) IsNot Nothing\line     ' ...\line Loop\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 List(Of T) append operator and rich indexers\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 The core List(Of T) overloads +, so l += item appends, and it exposes Python-like slice/negative indexers:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Language\line \line Dim l As New List(Of String)\line l += "a"\line l += "b"\line l += "c"\line \line Dim last = l(-1)          ' "c"\line Dim slice = l(0, 2)       ' \{ "a", "b" \}\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 LINQ-style sequence helpers\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Language\line Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Linq\line \line ' 100.Sequence -> 0 .. 99\line Dim squares = 100.Sequence _\line     .Select(Function(i) i * i) _\line     .ToArray\line \line For Each x In New List(Of Integer)(\{1, 2, 3\}).IteratesALL\line     Call Console.WriteLine(x)\line Next\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Unix-shell style helpers \u8212? UnixBash\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Language\line \line ' list files, recursively, long format \u8212? mirroring the `ls -l -r` shell command\line Dim files = (ls - l - r)  _\line     .Select(Function(path) path.FullName) _\line     .ToArray\line \line Dim text = cat("data/notes.txt")   ' read a whole file as one string\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 println and the application host\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.App\line \line Call println("hello from sciBASIC#")\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Vectorized array math (scripts & runtime)\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Numeric vectors participate in arithmetic directly; the runtime dispatches to the SIMD kernels:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Dim x = \{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\}\line Dim y = \{2, 3, 4, 5, 1\}\line \line Dim sum = x + 5                  ' => VecAddScalar(Of Integer)(x, 5)\line Dim z = (x * y + 6) / (x + y)    ' whole expression tree expanded element-wise\line \line Call print(x.Average())          ' [1] 3\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Inside a vbs script this rewriting is automatic; in a compiled project the same operators are available through the Microsoft.VisualBasic.Math.SIMD.Vectorization vocabulary.\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 Examples by Domain\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Tabular data & file I/O (Data/)\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.Framework.IO\line Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.Framework.StorageProvider\line \line ' Load a CSV into an in-memory dataframe resolver:\line Dim df = DataFrameResolver.Load("data.csv")\line \line ' Strongly-typed loading into entity objects (confirmed API):\line Dim people = EntityObject.LoadDataSet(Of Person)("people.csv")\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Reading a NetCDF scientific file:\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.BinaryData\line \line Dim nc = netCDFReader.Open("model.nc")\line Dim v = nc.getDataVariable("temperature")   ' ICDFDataVector\line Dim data = v.genericValue                   ' System.Array of the variable\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 The chain-style data-science pipeline (NumericTable)\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 See NumericTable above \u8212? load \u8594? cluster \u8594? reduce \u8594? plot \u8594? export in a single fluent chain, shared by every ML package.\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Deep learning training (Data_science/MachineLearning/)\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 See Deep Learning Suite for the CNN snippet; GNN, LNN and SNN follow the same add-layer \u8594? compile \u8594? train pattern (SGD/Adam), each with its own focused package.\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 LLM inference (llm/)\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 See LLM Engine \u8212? MoE routing, KV-cache decoding and schema-constrained function calling with a complete agent loop.\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 GPU kernels (cuda/)\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 See GPU Acceleration \u8212? either hand-written .cu kernels registered via KernelSources, or plain .NET methods translated to CUDA through IL2Cuda.\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Natural-language processing\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 TextRank keyword extraction (Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.NLP.TextRank + NLPExtensions):\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.NLP.TextRank\line Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.NLP.NLPExtensions\line \line ' Build the TextRank word graph, then rank it with PageRank:\line Dim doc As String = IO.File.ReadAllText("paper.txt")\line Dim graph = doc.TextGraph()          ' WeightedPRGraph (a GraphMatrix)\line Dim keywords = graph.KeyWords()      ' Dictionary(Of String, Double): word -> score\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 GraphQuery \u8212? a GraphQL-like DSL over your .NET objects (Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.GraphQuery):\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.GraphQuery\line \line <GraphQuery("gene")>\line Public Class Gene\line     <GraphQuery("symbol")> Public symbol As String\line     <GraphQuery("length")> Public length As Integer\line End Class\line \line ' Project only the requested fields from any object graph:\line Dim q = GraphQuery.DoQuery("gene \{ symbol length \}")\line Dim out = q.From(myGene)\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 See Data/GraphQuery/README.md and Data/TextRank/README.md for the full reference.\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Mathematics & ODEs (Data_science/Mathematica)\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Solve a system of ordinary differential equations by subclassing ODEs (namespace Microsoft.VisualBasic.Math.Calculus.Dynamics):\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Math.Calculus.Dynamics\line Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Math.LinearAlgebra\line \line Public Class Lorenz : Inherits ODEs\line     Public x, y, z As var\line     Public a As Double = 10\line     Public b As Double = 8 / 3\line     Public c As Double = 28\line \line     ' Initial values of the state variables.\line     Protected Overrides Function y0() As var()\line         Return \{New var("x", 0), New var("y", 1), New var("z", 0)\}\line     End Function\line \line     ' The differential equations: dy/dt = f(t, y).\line     Protected Overrides Sub func(dx#, ByRef dy As Vector)\line         dy(0) = a * (y - x)\line         dy(1) = x * (c - z) - y\line         dy(2) = x * y - b * z\line     End Sub\line End Class\line \line ' Integrate for 10000 steps over t in [0, 30]:\line Dim result = New Lorenz().Solve(10000, 0, 30)\line ' result.x -> time grid;  result.y -> Dictionary(name -> trajectory)\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Machine learning & data mining (Data_science/)\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.DataMining.KMeans\line \line ' source: IEnumerable(Of T) where T carries a numeric feature vector\line ' (T : EntityBase(Of Double)).\line Dim clusters = New KMeans().ClusterDataSet(source, k:=3)\line \line For i As Integer = 0 To clusters.NumOfCluster - 1\line     Dim centroid = clusters(i).ClusterMean()   ' centroid of cluster i\line     Console.WriteLine($"cluster \{i\}: \{String.Join(",", centroid)\}")\line Next\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Evolutionary search with Darwinism (genetic algorithm):\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.MachineLearning.Darwinism.GAF\line \line ' 1. Implement the fitness function (smaller value == better):\line Public Class MyFitness : Implements Fitness(Of MyChromosome)\line     Public ReadOnly Property Cacheable As Boolean = False\line     Public Function Calculate(c As MyChromosome, parallel As Boolean) As Double _\line         Implements Fitness(Of MyChromosome).Calculate\line         Return -EvaluateModel(c)\line     End Function\line End Class\line \line ' 2. Build a Population(Of MyChromosome) and evolve it generation by generation:\line Dim ga As New GeneticAlgorithm(Of MyChromosome)(population, New MyFitness())\line For i As Integer = 1 To 500\line     ga.Evolve()          ' advance one generation\line Next\line Dim best = ga.Best       ' the fittest chromosome\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 Visualization & "Graphics Artist" (Data_science/Visualization, gr/)\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.ChartPlots\line Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.Imaging\line \line ' 3-D scatter heatmap -> saved as a high-resolution raster image.\line Call Plot3D.ScatterHeatmap _\line     .Plot(data, size:=New Size(1200, 800)) _\line     .Save("scatter3d.png")\line \line ' 2-D scatter heatmap.\line Call ScatterHeatmap.Plot(points, gridSize:=20).Save("heatmap.png")\line \line ' Bar plot directly from a CSV.\line Dim bars = csv.LoadBarData("counts.csv")\line Call BarPlot.Plot(bars).Save("bars.png")\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Network / force-directed layouts and SVG/d3js export are provided by the Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.visualize.Network and colorbrewer modules \u8212? see gr/network-visualization/README.md.\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb160\sa80\plain\f1\fs36\b\cf1 Example for Draw sciBasic Logo\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Dim logo As Image, fontName$ = FontFace.Verdana\line Dim color1 As New SolidBrush(Color.FromArgb(0, 65, 102))\line Dim color2 As New SolidBrush(Color.FromArgb(0, 172, 221))\line \line Using g As IGraphics = DriverLoad.CreateDefaultRasterGraphics(New Size(900, 800), fill_color:=Color.Transparent)\line     Dim isometricView As New IsometricEngine(ambientStrength:=0.05, lightIntensity:=0.1)\line \line     isometricView.Add(New Knot(New Point3D(1, 1, 1), scale:=1), GREEN)\line     isometricView.Draw(g)\line \line     logo = DirectCast(g, GdiRasterGraphics).ImageResource.CorpBlank(blankColor:=Color.Transparent)\line End Using\line \line Using g As IGraphics = DriverLoad.CreateDefaultRasterGraphics(New Size(2400, 500), fill_color:=Color.Transparent)\line     Call g.DrawImageUnscaled(logo, New Point(50, 50))\line \line     Call g.DrawString("sci", New Font(fontName, 140), color1, New PointF(430, 90))\line     Call g.DrawString("BASIC#", New Font(fontName, 200), color2, New PointF(670, 60))\line     Call g.DrawString("http://sciBASIC.NET", New Font(FontFace.SegoeUI, 48), color1, New PointF(720, 350))\line \line     Call g.Flush()\line \line     Call DirectCast(g, GdiRasterGraphics).ImageResource _\line         .CorpBlank(blankColor:=Color.Transparent, margin:=30) _\line         .SaveAs("logo.png")\line End Using\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa80\plain\f1\fs40\b\cf8 LLM proxy (Microsoft.VisualBasic.LLMs, core)\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb120\sa120\cbpat9\chshdng0\plain\f2\fs20\cf4 Imports Microsoft.VisualBasic.LLMs\line \line ' Bridge a local Ollama (or any Func(Of String, String)) endpoint in:\line HookOllama(Function(prompt) MyLocalModel.Ask(prompt))\line \line ' Prompt the hooked model from anywhere in your code:\line Dim answer As String = Await LLMsTalk("Explain principal component analysis")\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
\pard\ql\sl276\slmult1\sb200\sa120\plain\f1\fs44\b\cf1 FAQ\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Why VisualBasic for scientific computing? Because the language is concise and readable, and sciBASIC# turns it into a productive environment for writing headless, reproducible data-science programs \u8212? without giving up the .NET ecosystem.\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Are the figures usable in a paper? Yes. The Imaging / ChartPlots engines are tuned for printable, publication-quality output and can export SVG, PDF and high-DPI raster images, which is why sciBASIC# is often described as the "Graphics Artist" for scientific plotting.\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Is it cross-platform? Yes. The core and math libraries target net10.0 and run on .NET under Windows, Linux and macOS. The graphics/imaging projects additionally target net10.0-windows. The cuda/ layer requires an NVIDIA GPU and is compiled for x64; everything else runs CPU-only.\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 Do the deep-learning models need PyTorch/TensorFlow installed? No. All neural networks (CNN/RNN/Transformer/GNN/LNN/SNN) and the LLM engine are pure managed implementations. If an NVIDIA GPU is present, ILCudaTensor can transparently move tensor math to the GPU; otherwise everything runs on the SIMD-accelerated CPU path.\par
\pard\ql\sl360\slmult1\sb0\sa120\plain\f0\af1\fs22\cf2 CLI or GUI? CLI-first and script-first. sciBASIC# is designed for command-line data-science applications \u8212? and with the vbs script engine you can even skip the project entirely and just run a .vb file.\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf2\par
